# Deliberately NO bare `data` entry.
#
# It was here to keep the local SQLite directory out of the image, and it also
# excluded src/app/(app)/data, src/app/api/data and src/components/data — so the
# CSV import/export screen 404'd in production while working locally.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, a leading slash does not fix this: Docker disregards
# leading and trailing slashes in ignore patterns, so `/data` and `data` mean
# the same thing. The `*.db*` patterns below already keep the database itself
# out at any depth, which is all that was ever needed.

node_modules
.next
.git
.github
.claude
docs/screenshots
test-results
playwright-report
coverage

# The database, wherever it lives. This is what `data` was really for.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.env
.env*.local
npm-debug.log*

